# Two-server llama-server.log slice for the Qwen3-only seconds basis
# (LP-0MW957SKX0079QKC).
#
# In router mode the parent announces each child:
#
#   srv load: spawning server instance with name=Qwen3 on port <n>
#   srv load: spawning server instance with name=mxbai-embed on port <m>
#
# Child lines carry a ``[<port>]`` prefix; eval-timing lines carry no
# timestamp. Both children emit ``prompt eval time`` lines, and the embeddings
# child runs at roughly half Qwen3's rate. A naive median over every line is
# therefore polluted (LP-0MW7V2D13004ZO65: ``seconds_basis_tok_s = 128.4``
# mixed ~102 tok/s embeddings lines with ~250 tok/s Qwen3 lines).
#
# Ground truth for the assertions:
#   Qwen3 (port 32999) prompt-eval rates: 240, 246, 250, 254, 260 tok/s
#       -> median 250.0 tok/s  (the honest basis)
#   Embeddings (port 51973) prompt-eval rates: 100, 101, 102, 103, 104 tok/s
#       -> must be excluded
#   Naive all-lines median (10 samples):
#       sorted 100, 101, 102, 103, 104, 240, 246, 250, 254, 260
#       -> (104 + 240) / 2 = 172.0 tok/s  (the polluted figure this fixes)
srv          load: spawning server instance with name=Qwen3 on port 32999
srv          load: spawning server instance with name=mxbai-embed on port 51973
